I did a slight variation of this. My monk couldn't teleport, so he didn't
put that middle boulder there to prevent the monsters from escaping
 - some heavy unliftable foos escaped a couple of squares, but I
didn't mind.

The altar was against the south wall of the room. On the north
side, a couple of squares away, against a dungeon wall,
I dug a hole through the floor. Now I could empty the
altar of unwanted junk by kicking the stuff into the hole.
(I like to keep altars tidy. Huan Ti must have appreciated it.)
I could have kicked the junk under a boulder, too, but a
giant might have picked it up. A couple of monsters escaped
through the hole, however. Perhaps an extra boulder blocking
the route to the hole would have made the nearly de-luxe
altar room more complete.

By the way, a staircase down was on the left from the altar,
and I had a boulder on the staircase, of course, so the
hole nearby was in any case mildly useful.

